Atlas overlay patch 0062: security/password-saving-default-on
Why: the inherited default-pref patch registers "offer to save passwords" as off, which was moot while
the credential block (dropped in atlas/drop.list) forced it off anyway. With the block gone the person
should be offered to save a password on a login form without first finding a switch, and what is saved
is encrypted with the login keyring key (reel scene 8). The default itself changes, so existing profiles
get it too and the switch in the password page still turns it off. A first-run preference reaches new
profiles only and stores an explicit value; the privacy defaults 0001-0005 are done the same way. Auto
sign-in stays off (the inherited default).
Files: components/password_manager/core/browser/password_manager.cc
Test filter: *PasswordManager*; journey atlas-keyring (the save bubble is offered on a local login form)
Rebase risk: L (one value, next to the line the inherited default-pref patch changes)
Release: 0.13
License: GPL-3.0-or-later (hunk in a file the inherited series patches)
Verified at: 156.0.8078.79, prepared tree with the inherited and platform series applied

